@title Lease or buy the new digital press
@subtitle Orchard Press commercial print shop
@author Lucinda Marsh, Owner
@date 2026-11-12

kpi Lease costs more over four years | $17,600 | vs buying | bad

The new press prints about 2.4 million pages a month. We compare two options over a four-year horizon. We recommend the lease, and it costs $17,600 more.

## Options

cards

### Buy

- Purchase price: $412,000
- Service contract: $14,400 a year ($57,600 over four years)
- Expected resale value after four years: $120,000
- Net four-year cost: $349,600

### Lease

- $7,650 a month for 48 months: $367,200
- Service included
- Deposit of two monthly payments: $15,300
- Optional buyout at the end: $95,000
- Net four-year cost: $367,200

## Four-year cost

data net = option,net four-year cost; Buy,349600; Lease,367200

chart bar net unit=$ labels title="Net four-year cost"

table = option,outlay,service,resale,net four-year cost; Buy,"$412,000","$57,600","-$120,000","$349,600"; Lease,"$367,200 in payments",included,none,"$367,200"

! The lease costs $17,600 more over four years but needs no large cash outlay.

## Risks

- Buying ties up cash we need for the new bindery, and the resale value is a guess.
- The lease locks us in for 48 months, although the buyout price is fixed today.

## Recommendation

We recommend the **lease**. It costs $17,600 more over four years ($367,200 against $349,600), and we accept that in exchange for keeping cash free for the new bindery.
